cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CLAIMS-Bench: Characterizing Language-model Agents' Implicit Moral and Stakeholder Commitments"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Yi
    given-names: Long
repository-code: "https://github.com/longyi1207/claims-bench"
url: "https://github.com/longyi1207/claims-bench"
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0-dev
date-released: 2026-07-16
keywords:
  - AI alignment
  - evaluation
  - value pluralism
  - AI safety
  - moral values
  - Schwartz basic values
  - revealed preference
abstract: >-
  Normative evaluation framework for AI assistants with two layers: L1
  stakeholder-fairness diagnostics (208 items, Gabriel & Keeling 2025
  fair-treatment-of-claims framework) and L3 value revelation (80 items,
  Schwartz 2012 basic-values backbone + Berlin pluralism), the current
  north star — characterizing models' implicit value commitments under
  radical under-specification and comparing to human pluralism, not
  certifying moral correctness.
